"id": "aorist",
"el": "Ο αόριστος",
"title": "The simple past (aorist)",
"span": "A2–B1",
"blurb": "The past endings and the augment, how to form the aorist stem from the present (-σα, -ψα, -ξα, -ησα, -ασα, -εσα), and when Greek uses the aorist where English says \"have done\".",
"intro": [
{
"p": "The aorist is the Greek simple past: **έφαγα** \"I ate\", **πήγαμε** \"we went\", **είδες;** \"did you see?\". It is the most frequent past tense, used for every completed event. It is formed from the **aorist stem** plus the past endings, with an **augment έ-** when the word would otherwise be too short to carry the stress."
},
